.TH KAGI-INSTALL 1 "September 2026" "Kagi 0.38.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kagi-install \- initialize a Kagi node and optionally bootstrap remote hosts over SSH
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kagi-install
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates local configuration/state directories, installs binaries/service files, generates node post-quantum identity material, initializes cluster credentials as appropriate, starts the service, and can repeat bootstrap steps on additional SSH-accessible hosts.
.SH SECURITY
Transferred bootstrap credentials are sensitive. Use trusted SSH host keys and remove temporary copies after installation.
.SH SEE ALSO
kagi-cluster-host(1), kagi-config(1)
